DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The iissuuppppeerr() and iissuuppppeerr__ll() functions test for any upper-case letter.
     The value of the argument must be representable as an _u_n_s_i_g_n_e_d _c_h_a_r or
     the value of EOF.

     In the ASCII character set, this includes the following characters (with
     their numeric values shown in octal):

     101 ``A''     102 ``B''     103 ``C''     104 ``D''     105 ``E''
     106 ``F''     107 ``G''     110 ``H''     111 ``I''     112 ``J''
     113 ``K''     114 ``L''     115 ``M''     116 ``N''     117 ``O''
     120 ``P''     121 ``Q''     122 ``R''     123 ``S''     124 ``T''
     125 ``U''     126 ``V''     127 ``W''     130 ``X''     131 ``Y''
     132 ``Z''

     The iissuuppppeerr__ll() function takes an explicit locale argument, whereas the
     iissuuppppeerr() function uses the current global or per-thread locale.

